{"id":"CVE-2007-3743","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-08-03T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T14:28:51.947Z","description":"Stack-based buffer overflow in bookmark handling in Apple Safari 3 Beta before Update 3.0.3 on Windows allows user-assisted remote attackers to cause a denial of service (application crash) or execute arbitrary code via a bookmark with a long title.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://osvdb.org/40882","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"40882"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1018495","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1018495"},{"url":"http://docs.info.apple.com/article.html?artnum=306174","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/35712","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"safari-bookmark-bo(35712)"},{"url":"http://isc.sans.org/diary.html?storyid=3214","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["apple","microsoft"]}
{"id":"CVE-2007-3944","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-07-23T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T14:37:05.370Z","description":"Multiple heap-based buffer overflows in the Perl Compatible Regular Expressions (PCRE) library in the JavaScript engine in WebKit in Apple Safari 3 Beta before Update 3.0.3, and iPhone before 1.0.1, allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via certain JavaScript regular expressions. NOTE: this issue was originally reported only for MobileSafari on the iPhone.  NOTE: it is not clear whether this stems from an issue in the original distribution of PCRE, which might already have a separate CVE identifier.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://docs.info.apple.com/article.html?artnum=306173","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/25002","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"25002"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/35577","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"iphone-safari-bo(35577)"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2007/2730","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2007-2730"},{"url":"http://www.securityevaluators.com/iphone/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1018439","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1018439"},{"url":"http://docs.info.apple.com/article.html?artnum=306174","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/26287","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"26287"},{"url":"http://www.nytimes.com/2007/07/23/technology/23iphone.html?_r=1&adxnnl=1&adxnnlx=1185163364-1OTsRJvbylLamj17FY2wnw&oref=slogin","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2007/2731","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2007-2731"},{"url":"http://www.securityevaluators.com/iphone/exploitingiphone.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["apple"]}
{"id":"CVE-2007-4424","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-08-18T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T14:53:55.862Z","description":"Apple Safari for Windows 3.0.3 and earlier does not prompt the user before downloading a file, which allows remote attackers to download arbitrary files to the desktop of a client system via certain HTML, as demonstrated by a filename in the DATA attribute of an OBJECT element. NOTE: it could be argued that this is not a vulnerability because a dangerous file is not actually launched, but as of 2007, it is generally accepted that web browsers should prompt users before saving dangerous content.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/476675/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20070811 Safari for windows remote arbitry file upload"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/477180/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20070820 Re: Re: Safari for windows remote arbitry file upload"},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/securityalert/3022","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SREASON"],"name":"3022"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1018575","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1018575"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/476690/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20070815 Re: Safari for windows remote arbitry file upload"}],"vendors":["apple","microsoft"]}
